<title>HONG KONG: H.K. dlr March M-3 rises 18.4 pct on year.</title>
<headline>H.K. dlr March M-3 rises 18.4 pct on year.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Monetary Authority gave the following money supply figures as percentage changes:</p>
<p>				   Mar '97    Feb '97     Mar '96</p>
<p> HK dollar M-3 (year-on-year)  +18.4	+22.3	 +15.4</p>
<p> HK dollar M-3 (month)	    -2.1	 +3.1	  +1.1</p>
<p> HK dollar M-1 (year-on-year) +13.2	+13.6	  +1.1</p>
<p> HK dollar M-1 (month)	   -4.6	 -5.9	  -4.3</p>
<p> HK dollar M-2 (year-on-year) +18.5	+22.6	 +15.8</p>
<p> HK dollar M-2 (month)	   -2.2	 +3.2	  +1.2</p>
<p>Loans to finance visible trade of Hong Kong (year-on-Year)</p>
<p>				    +3.6	 +2.9	 +12.9</p>
<p>Other loans for use in Hong Kong (year-on-year)</p>
<p>				   +23.4	+24.9	 +11.7</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong nesroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
